# UI Dashboard

Dark-themed Streamlit dashboard for the IO Workload Platform.

## Where to put these files

Drop the `ui/` folder directly into your repo root:

```
io-workload-platform/
├── ui/
│   ├── .streamlit/
│   │   └── config.toml      ← theme (dark, cyan accent, monospace)
│   ├── Home.py              ← entry point / overview
│   └── pages/
│       ├── 1_Classify.py    ← workload classifier
│       ├── 2_Hotspot.py     ← hotspot detection
│       ├── 3_Forecast.py    ← capacity & latency forecast
│       ├── 4_Rebalancer.py  ← move planner
│       ├── 5_Pipeline.py    ← run training / eval / backfill
│       └── 6_Data_Explorer.py  ← data viz & correlation
├── agents/
├── ml/
... (rest of repo unchanged)
```

## Install

```bash
pip install streamlit plotly
```

Both are already in `requirements.txt` — if you've run `pip install -r requirements.txt` you're good.

## Run

Always launch from the **repo root** so platform imports resolve:

```bash
cd /path/to/io-workload-platform
streamlit run ui/Home.py
```

Opens at **http://localhost:8501**

## Pages

| Page | What it does |
|---|---|
| 🏠 **Overview** | Live cluster snapshot — node utilization bars, workload mix donut, node table |
| 🔍 **Classify** | Enter IOPS/latency/throughput → get predicted workload class with confidence bars. Presets for each class. Works with trained model or rule-based demo. |
| 🔥 **Hotspot** | Rule-based + ML scoring with severity gauge. Normal / Warning / Critical scenario buttons. |
| 📈 **Forecast** | Capacity DTF, bandwidth demand, latency risk with time-series charts. Scenario picker. |
| ⚖️ **Rebalancer** | Interactive node + volume builder → Sankey flow diagram of move plan. Dry-run only. |
| 🚀 **Pipeline** | Run backfill / train / evaluate / hotspot training / full pipeline with live log output. |
| 📊 **Data Explorer** | Class distributions, per-class box plots, scatter explorer, correlation heatmap. Upload your own CSV. |

## Notes

- **No trained model?** Classify and Hotspot pages fall back to rule-based demo mode with a clear info banner.
- **Kafka / Redis offline?** Sidebar shows OFFLINE badges — all pages still work on local files.
- **Streamlit reruns on every widget interaction** — all computations are fast (< 200ms) except Pipeline steps which shell out to subprocess.
